Problem 1 - Duplicate AutoGoal Creation due to Lacking Highlight Tracking

**The problem:** When the 24h AutoGoal job finally runs, it never asks Reddit “is there already a valid Subscriber Goal in Community Highlights?” It only looks at Redis-tracked candidates (`findNewerClassicGoal` / Tiny-CTA protection). If that Redis view doesn’t show a newer classic—or the live highlighted goal isn’t reflected there—it proceeds to create and highlight a new goal anyway.

**What goes wrong in practice**

1. A completed goal’s AutoGoal timer comes due.
2. Pre-create checks pass using Redis state only (no Highlights read).
3. `createSubscriberGoal` submits a new “Welcome to r/…” post.
4. Only **after** that does `highlightAndVerifyPost` touch Highlights—to pin the new post and possibly unhighlight older managed ones.

So a still-valid highlighted goal can sit in Highlights while AutoGoal creates a second App post ~24h later. The system treats “Redis doesn’t know a newer successor” as “safe to create,” not “confirm the live highlighted primary is still the incomplete goal.”

**Why that matches the screenshot pattern**
Two same-title App goals ~24h apart is exactly what you get when the timer fires without a live Highlights “already covered” gate: the older post remains in the subreddit, and a new AutoGoal is posted and highlighted on top of (or instead of) the prior one.

**Bottom line:** The missing piece isn’t scheduling or title text—it’s the absent final Highlights/valid-primary check right before create. Without it, AutoGoal can duplicate even when a good goal is already highlighted.


Problem 2 - Removal of the New Subreddit Detection and DM system

We are gracefully ending this system. If any existing cron jobs are in installed subreddits related to this they should be ended gracefully or not renewed.

This system is **server-only outbound outreach**. It does not touch the Phaser/React client. An external publisher writes discovery JSON into a wiki page; this app polls that page, queues spaced DM jobs, and optionally sends a 12-hour report.

---

## End-to-end flow

```
External publisher (PRAW / outside this repo)
  writes r/subscriber_goal_dev wiki: invite-new-subs-data
         │
         ▼
invite-new-subs-poll-job  ──► processInviteNewSubsPoll()
  reads 3 wiki pages:
    invite-new-subs          (gate: "enabled" / anything else)
    invite-new-subs-message  (5 DM templates JSON)
    invite-new-subs-data     (batch of new subreddits JSON)
         │
         ├─ baseline / skip / enqueue delivery jobs
         ▼
invite-new-subs-delivery-job ──► processInviteNewSubsDelivery()
  reddit.sendPrivateMessage(top moderator)
         │
         ▼
invite-new-subs-report-job ──► processInviteNewSubsReport()
  DM summary to u/Alan-Foster (if gate enabled)
```

**Host subreddit:** hard-coded `subscriber_goal_dev` (`inviteNewSubsHostSubreddit`). Poll/report no-op unless the job runs in that subreddit.

**Cron status:** poll/report crons are currently **paused** in `devvit.json` (tasks registered, no `cron`). Comment in tests: restore `*/1 * * * *` (poll) and `0 */12 * * *` (report) to re-enable. Delivery jobs are only scheduled via `scheduler.runJob` from the poller.

