## Wiki pages (all under `r/subscriber_goal_dev`)

| Wiki page | Constant | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `invite-new-subs` | `inviteNewSubsControlWikiPage` | Gate. Trimmed content must equal `"enabled"`. Otherwise poll returns `disabled` and writes Redis `invite_new_subs:gate_state:v1` = `disabled`. Report also checks this gate. |
| `invite-new-subs-message` | `inviteNewSubsMessageWikiPage` | JSON message config (`schemaVersion: 1`, **exactly 5** templates). Placeholders: `{{topModerator}}`, `{{subredditName}}`, `{{isNsfw}}`. Templates round-robin via Redis incr. |
| `invite-new-subs-data` | `inviteNewSubsDataWikiPage` | Discovery batch JSON from external publisher (`source: "reddit/subreddits/new"`, 1–25 subs). Schema v1 or v2 (v2 adds `publisherSessionId` / `publisherStartedAt`). |

The app **only reads** these pages via `reddit.getWikiPage`. It never writes them. Writers live outside this repo.

---

## Poll → queue → DM (core logic)

In `processInviteNewSubsPoll`:

1. Host check → control wiki → message wiki → data wiki.
2. Classify batch vs Redis seen/gate/batch-identity (baseline on first enable, publisher restart, full-unseen batch of 25, etc.).
3. For each **new** public candidate: look up subreddit + top mod → pick template → render body → `queue.schedule(job)`.
4. Queue: Redis ZSET, max depth **16**, jobs spaced **15s**, each entry becomes `scheduler.runJob({ name: "invite-new-subs-delivery-job", data, runAt })`.
5. Delivery: claim key + 30-day recipient cooldown → `sendPrivateMessage` → status `messaged` / `dm_failed` / `cooldown_suppressed` / `duplicate`.
6. Side paths: startup test DM to `r/SubGoal`, full-batch alert DMs when a 25-unseen baseline is detected.
7. Report: every 12h window, if gate enabled, DM counts to `Alan-Foster`.

